From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] No vsync

PortareOS has no vsync. Frames are timed at the core's rate (Sync to
Exact Content Framerate, 0018, 0019). On the variable refresh path -
runemu exports MESA_VK_WSI_DISPLAY_VRR=1 for it, which Mesa and
setsettings read as well - the panel follows them and the display
driver repeats them below its range; at fixed refresh, kept for
debugging timing, each frame is shown at the next refresh. The display
offers FIFO only and latches every flip at vblank, so nothing tears.

Vsync is off and Sync to Exact Content Framerate on after the config
loads, after an override is loaded or unloaded and after Reset to
Default Values. Both entries leave the menu (Video > Synchronization,
Latency, Frame Throttle), and with vsync off so do the settings that
need it, black frame insertion among them; a BFI value saved before is
cleared with the rest, since it would still turn the core-rate timed
presents off. The hotkey does nothing.

On the variable refresh path, content that does not fit twice into the
panel's rate, a few arcade boards at 60.1 to 63 Hz against 120.198, is
refused. drivers_init finds it from the content's rate; the core never
runs, "This game is not supported" shows for three seconds, and
RetroArch quits.

Signed-off-by: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
---
diff --git a/configuration.c b/configuration.c
--- a/configuration.c
+++ b/configuration.c
@@ -6040,8 +6040,43 @@
 #ifdef HAVE_CONFIGFILE
    config_parse_file(global);
 #endif
+   config_no_vsync(config_st);
 }
 
+/* PortareOS has no vsync. Frames are timed at the core's rate (Sync to
+ * Exact Content Framerate, 0018); on the variable refresh path the panel
+ * follows them and the display driver repeats them below its range, and
+ * at fixed refresh, kept for debugging timing, each is shown at the next
+ * refresh. Neither the menu, the hotkey, a saved override nor a reset to
+ * defaults turns vsync or black frame insertion on.
+ *
+ * runemu says which path a launch is on by exporting
+ * MESA_VK_WSI_DISPLAY_VRR, which Mesa and setsettings read too. On the
+ * variable refresh path content that does not fit twice into the
+ * panel's rate is refused (runloop_refuse_content). */
+bool config_vrr_path(void)
+{
+   const char *v = getenv("MESA_VK_WSI_DISPLAY_VRR");
+   return v && v[0] == '1' && v[1] == '\0';
+}
+
+void config_no_vsync(settings_t *settings)
+{
+   if (!settings)
+      return;
+   if (settings->bools.video_vsync || !settings->bools.vrr_runloop_enable)
+      RARCH_LOG("[Config] No vsync: vsync off, Sync to Exact Content Framerate on.\n");
+   settings->bools.video_vsync        = false;
+   settings->bools.vrr_runloop_enable = true;
+   /* Black frame insertion went with vsync. A value saved before would
+    * still turn the core-rate timed presents (0018) off and run the
+    * driver's BFI pass with its menu entry gone. The dark frames are
+    * only read inside that pass, clamped to it, so they can stay. */
+   if (settings->uints.video_black_frame_insertion)
+      RARCH_LOG("[Config] No black frame insertion.\n");
+   settings->uints.video_black_frame_insertion = 0;
+}
+
 #ifdef HAVE_CONFIGFILE
 #if defined(HAVE_MENU) && defined(HAVE_RGUI)
 static bool check_menu_driver_compatibility(settings_t *settings)
@@ -7463,6 +7498,7 @@
    else
       runloop_state_get_ptr()->flags &= ~RUNLOOP_FLAG_OVERRIDES_ACTIVE;
 
+   config_no_vsync(config_st);
    return true;
 }
 
@@ -7506,6 +7542,7 @@
    else
       runloop_state_get_ptr()->flags &= ~RUNLOOP_FLAG_OVERRIDES_ACTIVE;
 
+   config_no_vsync(config_st);
    return true;
 }
 
@@ -7628,6 +7665,8 @@
    if (!config_load_file(global_get_ptr(),
             path_get(RARCH_PATH_CONFIG), config_st))
       return false;
+
+   config_no_vsync(config_st);
 
    if (settings->bools.video_fullscreen != fullscreen_prev)
    {
